{
  "dom_id": "step-7793",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Using a Ratio to Compute a Denominator",
  "problem": "Adam has a cedar tree and willow tree in his garden. The ratio of the height of the cedar tree to the height of a willow tree is $8:5.$ If the height of the cedar tree is $24$ meters, what is the height of the willow tree?",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio ${\\color{blue}8}:{\\color{red}5}$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}8}}{{\\color{red}5}}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the height of the   cedar tree and the denominator represents the height of the  willow tree.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $24$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}8}\\times 3}{{\\color{red}5}\\times 3} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}24}}{{\\color{red}15}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if the height of the cedar tree is $24$ meters, the height of the willow tree is $15$ meters.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
